**Theorem 9.1 (contraction preserves assigned names and legal queries).**
Suppose a finite canonical assignment partitions $S_D$ into nonempty
fibers $B_e$, with complete native witnesses containing those fibers.
Apply RRN normalization and then Theorem 3.2 to each witness, with
$d=D,n=1$. On every original source use the unchanged assigned name
of $\pi_D(v)$. This has exactly the same complete attained alphabet
and the same assigned full-family fibers as the original canonical
assignment. Sufficient paid preparation bounds on every source are

$$
T\le2^D-1,\qquad Q\le D,\qquad A\le(D-1)2^D+1,
\tag{GDB.43}
$$

counting Reads, maximum submitted address length and total letters.
The late reader uses zero Reads or one actual original-root literal at
an existing retained phase owner, chosen before every authentic count.

The same witness replacement on $n$ public prefix-free actually present
blocks at roots $Ra_i$, $|a_i|\le H$, preserves any assigned joint
fibers and names. A sufficient acquisition scan has

$$
T\le n(2^d-1),\quad Q\le H+d,\quad
A\le n\big((H+1)(2^d-1)+(d-2)2^d+2\big).
\tag{GDB.44}
$$

Each late phase query is the literal $Ra_jq_c$ of its actual owner.
When $H+d\le D$, every block target lies in the original request
family. This assertion about block targets alone does not supply readers
for other targets without a full-family construction.

Proof. Read all actual $Rq$, $q\in W_D$, in a public fixed order
before any request, including absent replies. The acquired array
determines $\pi_D(v)$ and its public assignment name. Theorem 3.2
keeps each complete witness's solution set exactly; it is therefore
still correct on the same assigned subset $B_e$. Every name remains
attained because $\pi_D$ fixes $S_D$. Export only the fixed-width
name and isolate the acquired array, unexported replies, selection
workspace, control and transcripts under Assumption 1.3. Public
allocation and padded finite selection ensure no further surviving
distinction is accessible. No phase vector is exported.

After a target arrives, its transformed prescription is a constant or
$B_v(p_c(a_K))$. A constant needs zero Reads. Otherwise its phase
equals the actual reply at the existing owner $o_r$. Query that
original-root literal once and use the composed table to obtain the
full target factor. Canonicalization preserves both this reply and the
requested factor on every source in the assigned full-family fiber.
Equation (GDB.4) supplies every subsequent authentic-count reply.

There are $2^D-1$ scan words and their lengths sum to
$\sum_{l=0}^{D-1}(l+1)2^l=(D-1)2^D+1$, proving (GDB.43).
For present block roots, use only the actual words $Ra_iq$.
Their suffix lengths sum to $(d-2)2^d+2$, also at $d=1$,
giving (GDB.44). Their late query uses the public prefix of the
selected actual owner and one suffix, not a subtree input.

At every actually present occurrence, pairing homomorphism gives

$$
r_{\rho^kt}(Ra_iq)=r_{\rho^k(t|_{Ra_i})}(q)\qquad(k\ge0).
\tag{GDB.45}
$$

This is exactly the presence premise of `original_present_transport`
